        <p>Spared from Baron Haussmann’s sweeping 19th-century demolitions, Le Marais is one of the very few neighborhoods in Paris where you can still wander through narrow, cobblestone medieval alleyways lined with 17th-century aristocratic courtyards. Today, it stands as the pulsing cultural nexus of the capital, brimming with designer showrooms, third-wave coffee roasters, contemporary art galleries, and the historic Jewish and LGBTQ+ quarters.</p>

        <p><strong>Why It’s Perfect for First-Timers:</strong> You can step out of your boutique hotel and walk to the Louvre, Centre Pompidou, Notre-Dame Cathedral on Île de la Cité, and the majestic Place des Vosges in 10 to 15 minutes. Even late at night, the streets feel bustling, safe, and delightfully social.</p>

        <p><strong>The Only Drawback:</strong> Because of the medieval preservation, hotel rooms here are notoriously intimate, and historic buildings frequently lack elevators. Book well in advance to secure rooms on lower floors if stairs are a concern.</p>

