          <span style="background:rgba(200,164,92,0.12);color:#8A6A23;border:1px solid rgba(200,164,92,0.28);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:4px 12px;border-radius:999px;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;">DAY 03</span>
          Bohemian Montmartre &amp; Canal Saint-Martin Sunset
        </h3>
        <p><strong>Morning:</strong> Take Metro Line 12 up to Lamarck-Caulaincourt. Climb the quiet rear steps of Montmartre to reach Sacré-Cœur Basilica before the tour buses arrive. Wander down picturesque Rue de l’Abreuvoir past La Maison Rose.</p>
        <p><strong>Afternoon:</strong> Ride Metro Line 2 over to Canal Saint-Martin in the 10th Arrondissement. Browse indie bookshops, sip artisanal espresso at Ten Belles, and watch boats pass through the historic iron locks.</p>
        <p><strong>Evening:</strong> Settle in for dinner at a relaxed neo-bistro in the 11th Arrondissement (such as <em>Clamato</em> or <em>Le Chateaubriand</em>) pairing seasonal small plates with biodynamic French wines.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Day 4 -->
      <div class="roam-day-card" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);border-radius:16px;box-shadow:0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);padding:24px;margin-bottom:20px;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;">
          <span style="background:rgba(200,164,92,0.12);color:#8A6A23;border:1px solid rgba(200,164,92,0.28);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:4px 12px;border-radius:999px;font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;">DAY 04</span>
          Le Marais Hidden Courtyards &amp; Seine Cruise
        </h3>
        <p><strong>Morning:</strong> Explore the boutique maze of Le Marais. Pick up fresh pastries from Du Pain et des Idées or Poilâne, then sit under the 17th-century arcades at Place des Vosges, the oldest planned square in Paris.</p>
        <p><strong>Afternoon:</strong> Browse the contemporary exhibitions at the Centre Pompidou or the Picasso Museum, followed by falafel on Rue des Rosiers.</p>
        <p><strong>Evening:</strong> Conclude your stay with an unhurried sunset cruise along the Seine (Vedettes du Pont Neuf), watching the golden limestone monuments drift by under Paris's romantic historic bridges.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Heading 5: Airport Transit & Logistics -->
      <h2>5. Paris Airport Transit Hacks (CDG &amp; ORY into the City)</h2>

      <p>Arriving in Paris can be seamless or intensely frustrating depending on how well you prepare for airport transit. The city is served by two main international airports:</p>

      <h3>Charles de Gaulle Airport (CDG) — 25 km Northeast</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>RER B Train (Fastest &amp; Most Cost-Effective):</strong> Connects directly from CDG Terminal 2 and Terminal 1/3 to Gare du Nord, Châtelet-Les Halles, and Saint-Michel in 35–45 minutes. Cost is €11.80 one-way. Best for solo travelers and light packers.</li>
        <li><strong>Official Flat-Rate Taxis (Best for Luggage &amp; Groups):</strong> By French law, official taxis operating from airport ranks charge fixed, non-negotiable flat rates: <strong>€56 to the Right Bank</strong> and <strong>€65 to the Left Bank</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--gold);">⚠️ Scammer Warning:</strong> Never follow anyone inside the arrival terminal offering "taxi service" or "private car." Always walk directly outside to the designated official taxi queue staffed by uniformed dispatchers. Unauthorized drivers routinely scam unsuspecting tourists for €150–€200.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Paris Orly Airport (ORY) — 13 km South (The 2026 Transit Revolution)</h3>
      <p>Historically considered less convenient by public transit, Orly underwent a massive upgrade with the <strong>Metro Line 14 southern extension</strong>. Today, you can step off your flight at Orly and ride the driverless Metro Line 14 directly into Châtelet or Gare de Lyon in just <strong>25 minutes</strong> for €10.30. It is faster, cleaner, and more reliable than any airport train in Europe.</p>

